// Eraser diagram type: Flow Chart. Matches the POC exactly (local storage, Postgres as the queue).
direction down
colorMode pastel
styleMode shadow
typeface clean

User uploads CSV [shape: oval, icon: user, color: blue]
Create import row [icon: database, label: "Create import row (status uploading)"]

Upload stream loop [icon: repeat, color: blue] {
  Receive piece [icon: download, label: "Receive next piece of file"]
  Write piece [icon: hard-drive, label: "Write piece to local storage"]
  Update hash [icon: hash, label: "Update sha256 hash"]
  More bytes [shape: diamond, label: "More bytes?"]
}

Mark queued [icon: flag, label: "Import row status queued"]

Job queue [icon: shuffle, color: orange] {
  Push import_id [icon: send, label: "Push import_id (Postgres, FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)"]
}

Worker picks job [icon: cpu, color: purple, label: "Worker picks up import_id"]
Open file stream [icon: file-text, label: "Open file as a stream"]

Chunk loop [icon: repeat, color: green] {
  Read chunk [icon: layers, label: "Read next 10k rows"]
  Validate rows [icon: check-circle, label: "Validate rows"]
  Save chunk [icon: database, label: "Save chunk to contacts table"]
  Update progress [icon: activity, label: "Save checkpoint and progress in import row"]
  More rows [shape: diamond, label: "More rows?"]
}

Done [shape: oval, icon: check, color: green, label: "Import row status done"]

User uploads CSV > Create import row
Create import row > Receive piece
Receive piece > Write piece
Write piece > Update hash
Update hash > More bytes
More bytes > Receive piece: yes
More bytes > Mark queued: no
Mark queued > Push import_id
Push import_id > Worker picks job
Worker picks job > Open file stream
Open file stream > Read chunk
Read chunk > Validate rows
Validate rows > Save chunk
Save chunk > Update progress
Update progress > More rows
More rows > Read chunk: yes
More rows > Done: no
